1
00:00:14,973 --> 00:00:17,642
[soft beeping]

2
00:00:17,643 --> 00:00:19,770
[whooshing]

3
00:00:31,365 --> 00:00:34,409
[indistinct chatter]

4
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:39,539
- What now?

5
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,791
- Now we wait.

6
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:43,834
- How long before...

7
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:45,253
- I have no idea.

8
00:00:45,254 --> 00:00:47,046
Could be hours.
[device whirs]

9
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:49,006
- This doesn't feel right.

10
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:51,050
- Remember,
Robby talked about--

11
00:00:51,051 --> 00:00:53,678
- It still feels wrong.

12
00:00:53,679 --> 00:00:56,597
- OK. This is Roxie's decision.

13
00:00:56,598 --> 00:01:00,518
Everything else in her life is
out of her control except this.

14
00:01:00,519 --> 00:01:03,354
She wants to go out
on her own terms.

15
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:05,064
Very few of us get to do that.

16
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:06,942
- I should pick up
more patients.

17
00:01:11,697 --> 00:01:13,739
- So Adam lives at Middle Hill?

18
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:15,116
- He lives at Middle Hill.

19
00:01:15,117 --> 00:01:16,701
- And he's three years
older than you?

20
00:01:16,702 --> 00:01:19,036
- He's three years
older than me.

21
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:22,081
- And he asked you
to be his girlfriend

22
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,292
6 months ago?

23
00:01:24,293 --> 00:01:28,212
- He asked me to be
his girlfriend at game night,

24
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:29,880
and I said yes.

25
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:31,257
- Got a patient waiting
for a doctor.

26
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:32,550
Vertigo in 13.

27
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:34,303
- OK. I'll be right there.

28
00:01:35,387 --> 00:01:37,221
[door closes]

29
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:40,016
Did Adam ask you
if you wanted to have sex?

30
00:01:40,017 --> 00:01:43,352
- I--Mel, I don't know
if I can tell you.

31
00:01:43,353 --> 00:01:45,229
- Of course you can tell me.
I'm your sister.

32
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:47,106
- Well, it's private.

33
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:49,984
- Look, it's just--it's
really important that I know.

34
00:01:49,985 --> 00:01:51,777
- Why?
- Because.

35
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:54,572
- Well...[sighs]
I can tell Dr. Langdon

36
00:01:54,573 --> 00:01:56,407
because Dr. Langdon
is my doctor,

37
00:01:56,408 --> 00:01:58,618
but I don't think
I can tell you.

38
00:01:58,619 --> 00:02:00,077
- Becca, just tell me!

39
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:02,079
- Why are you yelling?
- I'm not yelling.

40
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:04,457
It's just--look, it's
really important that I know.

41
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:05,916
- You're definitely yelling.
- Becca--

42
00:02:05,917 --> 00:02:07,918
- Uh, maybe--maybe we should
step outside for a minute.

43
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:09,211
- Why won't you tell me?

44
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:11,547
- Dr. King.
- [crying]

45
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:13,591
- Why don't you get some air?

46
00:02:13,592 --> 00:02:16,594
- [crying]

47
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:17,888
- Sorry.

48
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,973
Sorry.

49
00:02:20,974 --> 00:02:22,225
[door closes]

50
00:02:25,354 --> 00:02:27,355
- Hey, have you seen any
of the X-ray techs around?

51
00:02:27,356 --> 00:02:28,482
- Nope.

52
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:31,484
- Got an update for me?

53
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:33,069
- I'm just checking in.

54
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:35,279
- What are the chances of me
getting out of here on time,

55
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,656
do you think?
- That's up to you, Cap.

56
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:37,782
We can handle this.

57
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:39,618
Question is, will you let us?

58
00:02:45,624 --> 00:02:47,667
How are you two getting along?

59
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:49,753
- I can play nice
for another two hours.

60
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:52,630
- [scoffs] OK.

61
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:54,131
- Kept calling me "Doc."

62
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:57,385
Didn't know he was the real doc
until a few months in.

63
00:02:57,386 --> 00:02:59,053
He was keeping his
secret life from me.

64
00:02:59,054 --> 00:03:00,304
- Hmm.

65
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:01,806
Where are we
with his chest X-ray?

66
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:04,809
- Uh, X-rays are still
six or seven behind.

67
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:06,395
- When's the last time
you checked?

68
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:09,188
- Maybe 10 minutes ago,
but I--

69
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:10,439
- Stay on them.
- Yeah.

70
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,816
- Come on,
give the kid a break.

71
00:03:11,817 --> 00:03:14,276
It says here it takes an hour
to get an X-ray.

72
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:15,444
- You're the first person

73
00:03:15,445 --> 00:03:16,779
who read this fucking thing
all day.

74
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,489
[shout in distance]

75
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:19,740
[chuckles]

76
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,702
Don't get me started on those.

77
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:25,329
- How are you feeling?

78
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,790
- I'm good.

79
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:30,000
- You know, I take Lexapro.

80
00:03:30,001 --> 00:03:32,336
It helps with panic attacks,
not just depression.

81
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:33,922
- Promise, I'm fine.

82
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:36,882
Sorry about that, Mrs. Torres.

83
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:38,175
- Are you OK?

84
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:39,343
I thought you were
going to pass out.

85
00:03:39,344 --> 00:03:40,678
- Yep, all good.

86
00:03:40,679 --> 00:03:42,848
Let's just pick up
where we left off.

87
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:47,184
- Mrs. Torres presents
with one week

88
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:48,853
of painful, swollen right calf.

89
00:03:48,854 --> 00:03:50,563
No trauma, no fever,

90
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:52,773
no history
of hypercoagulable state.

91
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:54,859
However, she did take
a 15-hour bus ride

92
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:57,528
from Orlando to Pittsburgh
last week.

93
00:03:57,529 --> 00:04:00,030
- Mrs. Torres,
we're concerned about

94
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,366
a possible blood clot
in your leg

95
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:04,535
that can lead
to serious complications.

96
00:04:04,536 --> 00:04:07,037
We need to do an ultrasound,
but no need to worry.

97
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:08,205
If it's positive,

98
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:09,665
we can treat
with a blood thinner.

99
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:10,875
- Bueno.

100
00:04:10,876 --> 00:04:12,042
If there's something
I've learned,

101
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:13,502
it's to stop worrying.

102
00:04:13,503 --> 00:04:16,381
Can all your worries add
a single moment to your life?

103
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:20,885
[bell dings]
- Fresh from the lab.

104
00:04:20,886 --> 00:04:22,720
They said one's critical.
- They're supposed to

105
00:04:22,721 --> 00:04:24,096
call those up.
- I know.

106
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,931
Every time they try,
the red phone's been busy.

107
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:27,057
- Jesus Christ.

108
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,976
This was resulted
25 minutes ago.

109
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,895
Sodium 112.

110
00:04:30,896 --> 00:04:32,897
Mohan!

111
00:04:32,898 --> 00:04:36,233
Sprinkle some salt on
your patient before he seizes.

112
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:37,526
- Where are we?

113
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:39,403
- Kidney stone patient's
not obstructed.

114
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:40,738
Just waiting on meds.

115
00:04:40,739 --> 00:04:42,281
Ortho is performing
the replantation

116
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,783
on our water slide trauma.

117
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:46,577
Our perforated diverticulitis
patient, Howard,

118
00:04:46,578 --> 00:04:47,870
made it through surgery.

119
00:04:47,871 --> 00:04:50,247
And I'm calling
the CYF resource navigator

120
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:51,707
to see if
we're getting anywhere

121
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:54,585
with emergency foster care
for Baby Jane Doe.

122
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:57,546
Other than that,
labs and X-rays are way behind,

123
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:59,883
but our Golden Girls are
getting their steps in.

124
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,928
- Does Robby usually leave
as soon as his shift ends,

125
00:05:03,929 --> 00:05:05,346
or does he like to stick around

126
00:05:05,347 --> 00:05:07,515
for all the handoffs
to night shift?

127
00:05:07,516 --> 00:05:09,433
- Depends,
but he's usually pretty good

128
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:11,393
about getting out of here.

129
00:05:11,394 --> 00:05:12,854
[bell dings]

130
00:05:14,064 --> 00:05:15,981
- Shortness of breath
in South 16.

131
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:17,943
He could totally decompensate.

132
00:05:19,444 --> 00:05:21,987
I'm hoping to catch another
intubation before 7:00.

133
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:24,657
One more gets me to three
in my first week.

134
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,284
Probably a record.

135
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:29,703
- I'm looking for an easy one.

136
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:32,873
[sighs] Shift ends in 2 hours.

137
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,793
- You're supposed to pick up
the stable patients in order.

138
00:05:35,794 --> 00:05:38,546
- Do you need a--
a second opinion on that?

139
00:05:38,547 --> 00:05:39,673
- No.

140
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,091
- Dr. McKay.
- Yeah.

141
00:05:42,092 --> 00:05:44,134
- A girl named Kiki came
into reception looking for you.

142
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:45,302
- Kiki?

143
00:05:45,303 --> 00:05:46,303
- She said
she'll be in the park.

144
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:47,638
- Yeah, great, thanks.

145
00:05:47,639 --> 00:05:50,809
[indistinct chatter]

146
00:05:52,102 --> 00:05:56,188
- Hey, I think the labs are
back on your PID patient.

147
00:05:56,189 --> 00:05:58,190
- Thanks. [sighs]

148
00:05:58,191 --> 00:06:00,317
- Is everything OK?

149
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:02,654
- Uh, fantastic.

150
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:07,241
- Langdon?

151
00:06:07,242 --> 00:06:10,327
- Kind of hoping
I would never see him again.

152
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:13,248
- Well, you know,
maybe he's changed.

153
00:06:15,959 --> 00:06:17,710
When you got a sec,
there's something--

154
00:06:17,711 --> 00:06:19,169
- Santos!

155
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:21,171
I need you to pick up
food poisoning in 12.

156
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:22,840
- Yeah, sure. Why not?

157
00:06:22,841 --> 00:06:24,216
- What?

158
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:25,843
No snark? No pushback?

159
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:27,177
What have you done with Santos?

160
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:29,263
- Only 2 hours to go.

161
00:06:29,264 --> 00:06:30,432
I surrender.

162
00:06:31,516 --> 00:06:33,434
- That's the spirit.

163
00:06:33,435 --> 00:06:34,978
[bell dings]

164
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:40,524
- How's Becca?

165
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:41,859
- She's good.

166
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:43,861
- I'm trying to call
her living community,

167
00:06:43,862 --> 00:06:45,821
but they are not picking up.

168
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,282
- Why you calling 'em?

169
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:51,327
- Because I don't know anything
about this Adam person.

170
00:06:51,328 --> 00:06:53,913
I mean, they've been dating
for 6 months, and--and--

171
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,831
and I don't know anything.

172
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,875
She never said anything
about wanting a boyfriend

173
00:06:57,876 --> 00:06:59,668
or even liking anyone.

174
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:02,296
- Yeah, but that doesn't mean
she hasn't thought about it.

175
00:07:02,297 --> 00:07:03,881
- No, I don't--I don't want
to think about my sister

176
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:05,674
thinking about having sex.

177
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:08,427
I mean, who's to say he didn't
take advantage of her?

178
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:10,304
Middle Hill just let it happen.

179
00:07:10,305 --> 00:07:11,639
Why didn't they tell me?

180
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:13,057
- Well, maybe they
didn't know about it.

181
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:15,392
- Six months,
they had to have known.

182
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:18,687
I just--maybe it was a mistake
choosing Middle Hill.

183
00:07:18,688 --> 00:07:21,398
I--I mean, we saw
a lot of good places,

184
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:23,442
but that--that is where
Becca wanted to go.

185
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:24,610
I--

186
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:27,237
- Are you Becca's
legal guardian?

187
00:07:27,238 --> 00:07:29,073
- No, I have durable
power of attorney.

188
00:07:29,074 --> 00:07:31,408
But we did this thing called
supportive decision-making,

189
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:32,910
where she can...

190
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:34,954
make her own decisions.

191
00:07:34,955 --> 00:07:36,622
- There you go.
[tires screeching]

192
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:38,582
- Well, this is different.
- Why?

193
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:40,084
- Because it is.

194
00:07:40,085 --> 00:07:43,254
I--
[horn honking]

195
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:46,423
[tires screeching]

196
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:48,593
- My son, he's--
he's not moving.

197
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,263
- OK.

198
00:07:53,264 --> 00:07:54,765
Come on, buddy.

199
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:55,934
Come on.

200
00:08:00,105 --> 00:08:02,022
I got a hot
and unresponsive child.

201
00:08:02,023 --> 00:08:03,148
I need a room, Dana.

202
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,442
- Trauma Two.

203
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:07,778
- We need a core temp ASAP.

204
00:08:07,779 --> 00:08:09,947
Hi, I'm Dr. Al-Hashimi.
Are you Mom?

205
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,782
- Brenda Azurmendi.
- And this is?

206
00:08:11,783 --> 00:08:13,742
- Micah.

207
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:15,285
- Has Micah been sick
with a fever?

208
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:16,829
- No. He was fine all day.

209
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,747
I found him in the car.

210
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:19,915
[beeping]

211
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:22,501
- Pupils are sluggish,
but reactive.

212
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,253
No reaction to pain.

213
00:08:24,254 --> 00:08:25,838
[chiming]

214
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:28,674
- Uh, airway is patent
with low tidal volume.

215
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:30,802
Uh, let's set up
for intubation.

216
00:08:31,845 --> 00:08:33,178
- Heart rate is
22 in 10 seconds.

217
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:35,639
That's 132.
- Do you know his weight?

218
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,349
- No.
- Joy, the Broselow.

219
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,393
- The what?
- The Broselow tape gives us

220
00:08:39,394 --> 00:08:41,478
all the drug doses
based on length.

221
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:42,563
- Assisting with ventilation.

222
00:08:42,564 --> 00:08:44,148
Somebody call respiratory.

223
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:45,816
- You said you just
found him in the car?

224
00:08:45,817 --> 00:08:47,526
- I was working in the garden

225
00:08:47,527 --> 00:08:49,319
while he rode his trike
in the driveway.

226
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:51,405
One minute he was there,
and then he wasn't.

227
00:08:51,406 --> 00:08:53,157
I--I thought he had gone
into the house,

228
00:08:53,158 --> 00:08:54,825
but I couldn't find him
anywhere.

229
00:08:54,826 --> 00:08:56,577
He must have gotten tired

230
00:08:56,578 --> 00:08:59,038
and--and climbed in
and fallen asleep.

231
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:01,749
By the time I found him,
I--I couldn't wake him up.

232
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:03,125
- How long was he in there?

233
00:09:03,126 --> 00:09:04,126
- Uh, m-m-maybe--

234
00:09:04,127 --> 00:09:06,295
maybe 15 minutes or--or 20.

235
00:09:06,296 --> 00:09:08,672
- And the car was
just unlocked?

236
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:10,132
- It's a safe neighborhood.

237
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:11,717
- Uh, Joy.

238
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:16,847
OK, so you're gonna want
to start at the head,

239
00:09:16,848 --> 00:09:20,059
measure the length,
and then read it off.

240
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,519
- Uh, approximate weight
is 25 kilograms.

241
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,354
- 250 bolus of LR.

242
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:26,190
- I have doses
for rock and ketamine.

243
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:28,525
- Almost no tone.
I can do this without meds.

244
00:09:28,526 --> 00:09:29,651
Uh, it's easy enough to bag.

245
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:30,861
Let's wait for RT.

246
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,488
- When the temperature
is this high,

247
00:09:32,489 --> 00:09:34,364
the muscles can lose
their strength,

248
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:36,408
so we're going to help him
breathe with a tube.

249
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:38,952
- Uh, rectal temp is 105.5.

250
00:09:38,953 --> 00:09:40,120
- Heatstroke.

251
00:09:40,121 --> 00:09:41,622
- Ice packs
to the groin and axilla.

252
00:09:41,623 --> 00:09:43,123
- See if we have an Arctic Sun
that's not in use.

253
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:44,667
We need all the ice we can get.

254
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:47,921
[softly]
And a pediatric body bag.

255
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:52,633
- Still waiting on
your ketorolac pills.

256
00:09:52,634 --> 00:09:54,218
I will keep following up
with the pharmacy.

257
00:09:54,219 --> 00:09:55,844
- I told my son
I would meet him at the park.

258
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:57,554
We always watch
the fireworks together.

259
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:58,555
- Sorry, Mr. Green.

260
00:09:58,556 --> 00:09:59,723
We won't forget about you.

261
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:00,975
- Mm.

262
00:10:05,105 --> 00:10:06,396
- Heard you had a heart attack.

263
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:08,483
- I did not have
a heart attack.

264
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,568
- Hey, Samira,
how are you feeling?

265
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:13,862
- I am totally fine.

266
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,030
- Uh, glad to hear it.

267
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,198
Hey, do you mind
watching my patients

268
00:10:16,199 --> 00:10:17,366
for 5 minutes?

269
00:10:17,367 --> 00:10:18,408
I have to step out for a sec.

270
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:19,701
- No problem.

271
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:22,371
- Ogilvie, you, uh,
want to get some air?

272
00:10:22,372 --> 00:10:23,622
Got a good case for you.

273
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:26,083
- Might an intubation
be required?

274
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:27,209
- No.

275
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:28,377
It's an unhoused patient

276
00:10:28,378 --> 00:10:30,255
I've treated
on the street team.

277
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:34,092
- Thank you so much.

278
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:43,977
- Hi, Becca.
- Hey.

279
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:56,780
- I'm sorry I yelled at you.

280
00:10:56,781 --> 00:10:59,158
I was just...

281
00:10:59,159 --> 00:11:00,450
surprised.

282
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:02,452
- The nurse said I can leave.

283
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:03,745
- Yeah, um,

284
00:11:03,746 --> 00:11:05,622
can we just finish
our conversation first?

285
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:07,583
- About what?

286
00:11:07,584 --> 00:11:09,793
- Look, I--I know you don't
have to tell me anything.

287
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:11,587
I just...

288
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:15,550
kind of hope you'd want to.

289
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:19,136
When Adam asked you
to have sex--

290
00:11:19,137 --> 00:11:20,804
- He didn't ask me.

291
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,348
I asked him.

292
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:24,975
- So he didn't pressure--

293
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:26,768
- No.

294
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,688
- So you wanted to have sex.

295
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:31,481
- I wanted to have sex.

296
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:32,816
Sex is great!

297
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,611
We talked about sex
in my mind and body class.

298
00:11:35,612 --> 00:11:37,405
I told my therapist too.

299
00:11:39,699 --> 00:11:41,533
- Hey, the, uh,
pancreatitis in North 3's

300
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:43,160
still waiting for you.
- OK.

301
00:11:43,161 --> 00:11:45,329
- Can I go now?
- Uh, just one second.

302
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:46,580
Uh, I'll be right there.

303
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:48,458
I'm just gonna
walk my sister out.

304
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:56,090
Yeah, sorry,
I'm right behind you.

305
00:11:58,092 --> 00:12:00,260
- Curtis Larson, 42.

306
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:01,887
Called to the golf course
for combative behavior

307
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:03,305
with his buddies.

308
00:12:03,306 --> 00:12:05,599
No signs of trauma,
just alcohol on the breath.

309
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,392
- Seems to have
calmed down a bit.

310
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:08,685
- He was fighting us so hard,

311
00:12:08,686 --> 00:12:10,229
had to give
4 milligrams of Versed

312
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:11,647
to get vitals and a line.

313
00:12:11,648 --> 00:12:13,732
Good BP, pulse ox 99
on two liters.

314
00:12:13,733 --> 00:12:15,150
- Between the booze
and the Versed,

315
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:16,568
he'll be sleeping it off
for a while.

316
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:18,237
- Central 14, guys.

317
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:21,115
[beeping]

318
00:12:24,369 --> 00:12:25,369
- [sighs]

319
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:26,579
Roxie's gone.

320
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,373
- Is the husband still
in there with her?

321
00:12:29,374 --> 00:12:31,166
- Yeah, Javadi's with him.

322
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:33,877
She needs a death note.
I can't find McKay.

323
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,212
- OK, I'll be right there.

324
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:36,421
- OK.

325
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:38,548
- Have you seen McKay anywhere?

326
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:39,926
- No.

327
00:12:42,553 --> 00:12:44,263
- Have you ever seen
a xylazine wound?

328
00:12:44,264 --> 00:12:46,306
- No.
- But you know what it is?

329
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:47,599
- Yes.

330
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,226
- Then you know
its street name is Tranq,

331
00:12:49,227 --> 00:12:50,227
and this shit is nasty

332
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:52,396
and can lead to skin necrosis.

333
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:54,731
- I've never understood
drug addiction.

334
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,900
- Well, you need to try.

335
00:12:56,901 --> 00:12:59,152
A little empathy goes
a long way in this job.

336
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,570
- I am empathetic, I ju--

337
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:01,989
I don't understand how
an intelligent person

338
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:04,324
allows themselves to--
- Can make mistakes?

339
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:06,076
Heal themselves?
Take away the pain?

340
00:13:06,077 --> 00:13:08,245
Hide from the abuse?

341
00:13:08,246 --> 00:13:11,248
We're healers, not judges.

342
00:13:11,249 --> 00:13:13,583
- Shouldn't we go
to the crosswalk?

343
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:14,918
No?

344
00:13:14,919 --> 00:13:16,461
OK, this is what we're doing.

345
00:13:16,462 --> 00:13:18,755
I see organ donation
in my future.

346
00:13:18,756 --> 00:13:20,382
Sorry!
[tires screeching]

347
00:13:20,383 --> 00:13:22,092
[horn honking]

348
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:25,263
[muffled chatter]

349
00:14:15,855 --> 00:14:18,148
- How's it going, Kiki?

350
00:14:18,149 --> 00:14:19,649
- Who's this?

351
00:14:19,650 --> 00:14:21,109
- Oh, it's, uh, Ogilvie.

352
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,487
He's a student doctor
here to help me.

353
00:14:23,488 --> 00:14:25,947
So what's happening with you?

354
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,657
- My leg's getting
stinky again.

355
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:29,993
- Yeah?
OK, let's take a look.

356
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,245
- [softly] OK.

357
00:14:35,166 --> 00:14:37,042
- Is that an injection site?

358
00:14:37,043 --> 00:14:38,794
- No.
- No.

359
00:14:38,795 --> 00:14:41,546
Xylazine wounds can
show up anywhere.

360
00:14:41,547 --> 00:14:43,507
You, uh--
you still using Tranq?

361
00:14:43,508 --> 00:14:44,925
- Sometimes.

362
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:46,760
- Sometimes is not good, Kiki.

363
00:14:46,761 --> 00:14:48,178
You know it's nasty stuff.

364
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:49,471
- I'm trying to quit.

365
00:14:49,472 --> 00:14:51,348
- How you going about that?

366
00:14:51,349 --> 00:14:53,517
- I go to meetings sometimes.

367
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:54,851
- Meetings are good.

368
00:14:54,852 --> 00:14:57,688
Uh, not using's even better.

369
00:15:00,066 --> 00:15:02,985
Uh, OK.
What's your plan, Ogilvie?

370
00:15:06,406 --> 00:15:08,031
Ogilvie, you OK?

371
00:15:08,032 --> 00:15:09,282
- Yes.
- Yeah?

372
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:10,450
- Absolutely.

373
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:15,247
Uh, my plan is
clean with saline.

374
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:16,415
Antibiotics?

375
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:18,542
- Medihoney to break down
the eschar.

376
00:15:18,543 --> 00:15:19,876
And then?

377
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:22,879
- Um, redress with Xeroform

378
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,172
and an ABD pad
and a Kerlix wrap.

379
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:25,715
- Yeah, that'll do it.

380
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,218
You need to change this
dressing every day, Kiki, OK?

381
00:15:28,219 --> 00:15:29,886
- I don't think I can do that.

382
00:15:29,887 --> 00:15:30,887
- We'll give you
all the supplies.

383
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:32,180
You can do it yourself.

384
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,890
You won't even have
to come back here.

385
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:36,726
- Yeah. OK.

386
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:38,728
- OK.

387
00:15:38,729 --> 00:15:40,148
OK, pass the saline.

388
00:15:46,779 --> 00:15:49,406
[indistinct chatter]

389
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:51,408
- Hey, I'm Dr. Whitaker.

390
00:15:51,409 --> 00:15:52,993
This is Dr. Santos.

391
00:15:52,994 --> 00:15:55,288
- Roberto.
Like Roberto Clemente.

392
00:15:56,456 --> 00:15:59,041
- Oh, sorry.
I--I don't know who that is.

393
00:16:00,001 --> 00:16:02,294
- Pirates Hall of Famer
Roberto Clemente.

394
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:04,380
You--you don't watch baseball?

395
00:16:05,590 --> 00:16:07,757
- Well, I am from Nebraska.

396
00:16:07,758 --> 00:16:10,343
We went to a few
Storm Chasers games as a kid.

397
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:11,428
That's about it.

398
00:16:11,429 --> 00:16:13,181
No Major League team, you know.

399
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:16,183
- All right.
What happened to your elbow?

400
00:16:16,184 --> 00:16:19,978
- [chuckles] Oneil Cruz hits
a walk-off tater, right?

401
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:23,106
And I--I--I catch it, you know,

402
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:24,900
um, but then somebody
fell on top of me,

403
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:26,651
and I--I think I heard a pop,

404
00:16:26,652 --> 00:16:28,904
but hard to tell
with all the screaming.

405
00:16:28,905 --> 00:16:30,655
- That sounds pretty dangerous.
- Yeah.

406
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:31,823
- You're not one of those guys

407
00:16:31,824 --> 00:16:34,493
who steals balls from kids,
are you?

408
00:16:34,494 --> 00:16:36,161
- I didn't steal this.
I wouldn't do that.

409
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:37,496
I would never do that.
I would never do that.

410
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:39,080
[scoffs]
- OK.

411
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:41,292
Can you move your fingers
for me?

412
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:45,962
- And the thumb?

413
00:16:45,963 --> 00:16:47,589
- Uh...

414
00:16:47,590 --> 00:16:48,924
No.
- OK, you know what?

415
00:16:48,925 --> 00:16:50,300
We can put that
in a belongings bag--

416
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:51,510
- [laughs] No, thanks.

417
00:16:51,511 --> 00:16:53,429
I, um--I think
I will hold on to this.

418
00:16:54,639 --> 00:16:55,972
- OK. Uh, you know what?

419
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:57,891
We can put you in a sling,

420
00:16:57,892 --> 00:16:59,476
and then you can
hold on to the ball

421
00:16:59,477 --> 00:17:00,728
while we examine you.

422
00:17:02,313 --> 00:17:04,481
- OK. Yeah, I guess.

423
00:17:04,482 --> 00:17:05,649
[grunts]

424
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:07,025
- Uh, you're gonna
throw in an IV

425
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,610
and start with 4 of morphine.

426
00:17:08,611 --> 00:17:11,071
- No, no, no, no.
I don't want to be knocked out.

427
00:17:11,072 --> 00:17:13,156
- No, it's a low dose.
You won't be knocked out.

428
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:14,574
It'll just help with the pain.

429
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:15,825
Might make you a little drowsy.

430
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:18,370
- No. I need to stay alert.

431
00:17:18,371 --> 00:17:19,663
- OK.

432
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:21,790
Uh, we will order you an X-ray.

433
00:17:21,791 --> 00:17:24,669
Just please let us know
if you change your mind.

434
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:27,045
- OK, yeah.

435
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:30,215
[beeping]

436
00:17:30,216 --> 00:17:32,968
- Temp is down to 103.5.

437
00:17:32,969 --> 00:17:34,886
- Long way to 98.6.

438
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:36,471
- 102, we take him
off the ice.

439
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:39,558
Otherwise, we can overshoot
and cause hypothermia.

440
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:41,351
I put in orders for CK.

441
00:17:41,352 --> 00:17:43,520
- What does the CK
tell us, Joy?

442
00:17:43,521 --> 00:17:46,481
- Rhabdo from muscle breakdown
can take out the kidneys.

443
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:49,026
- I'm more concerned
about his brain.

444
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:56,616
- It's two times a day
for three days,

445
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:58,451
and, uh, a nurse can
crush it up.

446
00:17:58,452 --> 00:18:00,704
- Dr. Langdon already told me.

447
00:18:00,705 --> 00:18:02,330
OK, bye, Mel.

448
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,790
- I'll see you, uh--
I'll see you at fireworks.

449
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:06,543
- Oh, I was going
to watch fireworks

450
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:09,129
with Adam and his parents.

451
00:18:09,130 --> 00:18:11,089
- Where?
- At the park.

452
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:13,717
They're picking us up.
They go every year.

453
00:18:13,718 --> 00:18:15,385
- But we always watch
the fireworks together.

454
00:18:15,386 --> 00:18:16,469
I have your headphones.

455
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:18,555
- Adam said that he has extra.

456
00:18:18,556 --> 00:18:21,474
- OK, well, um, do you have
Adam's parents' phone number?

457
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:22,642
- Why?

458
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:24,812
- Just in case
I need to reach them.

459
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:28,398
- I want to go now.

460
00:18:28,399 --> 00:18:30,735
- Well, I guess I could call--
- Bye, Mel!

461
00:18:33,404 --> 00:18:35,739
- So how long have you been
part of the street team?

462
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:37,907
- Oh, about a year.

463
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:39,576
- And why do you do it?

464
00:18:39,577 --> 00:18:42,412
- Oh, most of these unhoused
folks feel abandoned.

465
00:18:42,413 --> 00:18:43,455
Sorry.

466
00:18:43,456 --> 00:18:45,290
They, uh, don't trust easily.

467
00:18:45,291 --> 00:18:48,084
Meeting them where they're at
makes a big difference.

468
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:51,588
I've been trying to get Kiki
to come by for months.

469
00:18:51,589 --> 00:18:54,090
You should, uh, volunteer.

470
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:55,467
It's great training.

471
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,927
Street team could always
use the help.

472
00:18:57,928 --> 00:19:00,430
- Yeah, uh, maybe.

473
00:19:00,431 --> 00:19:01,806
- Thank you.

474
00:19:01,807 --> 00:19:03,933
Hey, how did the deposition go?

475
00:19:03,934 --> 00:19:06,603
- Um, I'm glad it's over,

476
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:09,356
but I didn't feel good
about it at all.

477
00:19:09,357 --> 00:19:11,107
You know, I'm still not
supposed to talk about it.

478
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:13,109
- No, but you can talk
about how you feel.

479
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:15,612
Who do you have to talk to when
things aren't going so good?

480
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:17,530
Friends? Family?

481
00:19:17,531 --> 00:19:18,865
- Actually, I don't really
have anyone--

482
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:20,367
- Hey, McKay,
where have you been?

483
00:19:20,368 --> 00:19:22,118
- Oh, I, uh--I stepped out.

484
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:23,870
- Did you tell anybody?

485
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,747
- Oh, I was, uh,
treating a young woman

486
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:26,998
I met on the street team.

487
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:28,917
- Did she check in
as a patient?

488
00:19:28,918 --> 00:19:31,337
- No, we treated her
in the park.

489
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:34,964
- "We"?

490
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:36,966
- I, uh--I took Ogilvie.

491
00:19:36,967 --> 00:19:39,177
- Oh, OK, so you treated her

492
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:41,304
outside the ED on PTMC's dime

493
00:19:41,305 --> 00:19:42,806
and you brought
a medical student with you,

494
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:44,349
right when we're in
the middle of crisis mode,

495
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,975
and we need all hands on deck.

496
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:47,268
- We were gone
for 10 minutes, tops.

497
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,687
- When you're here,
I need you to be here.

498
00:19:48,688 --> 00:19:51,982
And while you stepped out,
Roxie died.

499
00:19:53,359 --> 00:19:54,568
- What?

500
00:19:58,823 --> 00:20:01,408
Oh, man, I'm sorry.

501
00:20:01,409 --> 00:20:03,201
I didn't think she would
be gone that quickly.

502
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:04,995
- Shit.

503
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,248
- Excuse me.

504
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:11,251
Um, she took a nasty fall.
Her shoulder.

505
00:20:11,252 --> 00:20:12,669
Screamed in pain
when we put the ties on her.

506
00:20:12,670 --> 00:20:14,003
- Hello, I'm Dr. Robinavitch.

507
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:15,547
This is Dr. McKay.

508
00:20:15,548 --> 00:20:18,258
- Agents Correa and Russo.

509
00:20:18,259 --> 00:20:20,552
She needs to be looked at
before we process her.

510
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:22,138
- What's your name, ma'am?

511
00:20:23,764 --> 00:20:25,056
- Pranita.

512
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:27,726
- We're gonna take care of you,
OK?

513
00:20:27,727 --> 00:20:29,144
- You said she fell?

514
00:20:29,145 --> 00:20:31,479
- We were conducting
a sweep at her restaurant.

515
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,148
Everyone in the kitchen
took off.

516
00:20:33,149 --> 00:20:35,358
She was shoved down
some alley stairs.

517
00:20:35,359 --> 00:20:37,819
- Right.
- Could be a rotator cuff tear

518
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:40,488
or an AC separation.

519
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:42,240
- Let's put her in a chair,
find her a room.

520
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,951
- South 19.

521
00:20:48,330 --> 00:20:49,874
- Yeah. Just through here.

522
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:52,667
- Curtis, dude.

523
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:54,085
[chuckles] What happened?

524
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:55,920
- Medics had to sedate him
to transport.

525
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,255
- [sighs]

526
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:59,132
I didn't realize he was
such an angry drunk.

527
00:20:59,133 --> 00:21:00,425
- So you've seen him
drunk before?

528
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:02,719
- Sure, yeah,
but never like this.

529
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,763
He tried to pick a fight
with the guys in front of us.

530
00:21:04,764 --> 00:21:06,055
He said they were
going too slow.

531
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:07,974
That's when
they called the cops.

532
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:10,310
- Could he have taken drugs?

533
00:21:10,311 --> 00:21:12,395
- If he did, they were not
the performance-enhancing kind.

534
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,563
[chuckles]

535
00:21:13,564 --> 00:21:15,232
He shot a 112.

536
00:21:16,567 --> 00:21:19,652
- We'll order labs,
see what we can figure out.

537
00:21:19,653 --> 00:21:21,654
- Uh, any family
we can contact?

538
00:21:21,655 --> 00:21:23,615
- I have no idea.
We don't talk about that shit.

539
00:21:23,616 --> 00:21:24,991
How long is he gonna be here?

540
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:27,327
- At least 3 or 4 hours,
till he sobers up.

541
00:21:27,328 --> 00:21:28,620
- Cool.

542
00:21:28,621 --> 00:21:30,622
Is it OK if I just come back
around 9:00?

543
00:21:30,623 --> 00:21:32,666
- Sure.
- Great, thanks.

544
00:21:35,878 --> 00:21:38,631
- I need those removed
so I can check her vital signs.

545
00:21:41,634 --> 00:21:42,634
- [gasps]

546
00:21:42,635 --> 00:21:44,470
- OK, tender over the AC.

547
00:21:50,976 --> 00:21:53,269
- Can you, uh,
lift your right arm up

548
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:55,606
above your shoulder like this?

549
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:02,779
- Ah!
- Heart rate's 110.

550
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:03,863
Pulse ox 98.

551
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:05,949
- Painful arc test is positive.

552
00:22:05,950 --> 00:22:07,450
- Try the drop arm test.

553
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:10,328
- I'm gonna lift
your arm up, OK?

554
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:13,832
And you just lower it
as slowly as you can, OK?

555
00:22:13,833 --> 00:22:15,625
OK.

556
00:22:15,626 --> 00:22:18,211
Positive drop arm test.
- What's that mean?

557
00:22:18,212 --> 00:22:20,088
- That means that
she's gonna require an X-ray.

558
00:22:20,089 --> 00:22:22,006
It's most likely
a rotator cuff tear,

559
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:23,800
which sometimes can come
with a fracture.

560
00:22:23,801 --> 00:22:25,301
We need an X-ray
to rule it out.

561
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:27,220
- How long is that gonna take?

562
00:22:27,221 --> 00:22:28,930
- [sighs]
Our computers are down today.

563
00:22:28,931 --> 00:22:30,557
Everything's moving
a little slower than usual,

564
00:22:30,558 --> 00:22:32,141
but we will fast-track her.

565
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:34,435
- Is there anyone you want us
to call, Pranita?

566
00:22:34,436 --> 00:22:36,813
- No phone calls.

567
00:22:36,814 --> 00:22:38,566
Got a bathroom?

568
00:22:46,866 --> 00:22:48,325
- Right there.

569
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,286
- I do not want these guys here

570
00:22:51,287 --> 00:22:52,787
any longer than
they need to be,

571
00:22:52,788 --> 00:22:54,497
so let's find X-ray
and fast-track this one.

572
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:56,624
- Her family might be worried.
Maybe I can call them--

573
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:58,167
- No, no, no.
Just stay with her.

574
00:22:58,168 --> 00:22:59,502
Make sure she has
everything she needs.

575
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:00,962
We treat her injury,
and that's it.

576
00:23:00,963 --> 00:23:02,630
- OK.

577
00:23:02,631 --> 00:23:05,550
- Jamie Guerrero
to window three, please.

578
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:08,178
Jamie Guerrero to window three.

579
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:13,142
[indistinct chatter]

580
00:23:23,944 --> 00:23:27,156
[both speaking Spanish]

581
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:36,873
- Got a lateral.

582
00:23:36,874 --> 00:23:38,166
Best I could.

583
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:40,543
- Posterior dislocation,
no fracture.

584
00:23:40,544 --> 00:23:42,378
Thanks.
- Mm-hmm.

585
00:23:42,379 --> 00:23:43,838
- OK, good news, Roberto.

586
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:47,383
No broken bones, but the elbow
joint is dislocated

587
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:49,260
and we need to get the ball
back in the socket.

588
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:51,763
The best way is with
sedation and pain meds.

589
00:23:51,764 --> 00:23:53,765
- No, no, no.
- I know you said no morphine,

590
00:23:53,766 --> 00:23:55,850
but we can put local
anesthetic into the joint

591
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:56,935
to block the pain.

592
00:23:56,936 --> 00:23:58,102
That way you won't be sedated.

593
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:00,021
- No, thanks, Doc.
[chuckles]

594
00:24:00,022 --> 00:24:02,274
Just--just give me
a bullet to bite on.

595
00:24:07,071 --> 00:24:08,988
- They raided Joe's
over in Green Tree.

596
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:10,573
- Oh, man, I love that place.

597
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:11,908
- Brought in one
of the employees.

598
00:24:11,909 --> 00:24:13,076
- So ICE is here?

599
00:24:13,077 --> 00:24:14,410
People are leaving
the waiting room.

600
00:24:14,411 --> 00:24:15,995
Ten patients already.
What should I do?

601
00:24:15,996 --> 00:24:17,747
- Just tell them the truth
and hope they stay

602
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:18,998
for the treatment
that they need.

603
00:24:18,999 --> 00:24:20,416
- Martha took off.

604
00:24:20,417 --> 00:24:21,626
I'm gonna call her
when I get a chance.

605
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:23,127
- Oh, shit.
Yeah, make sure she's OK.

606
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:24,671
Will you call
the EVS department too

607
00:24:24,672 --> 00:24:25,922
and let 'em know?
- Will do.

608
00:24:25,923 --> 00:24:27,090
- All right,
hold down the fort.

609
00:24:27,091 --> 00:24:28,132
Let us know if you need backup.

610
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,509
- You got it.

611
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:32,095
- Can't we just tell
the agents to fuck off?

612
00:24:32,096 --> 00:24:34,639
- They are not gonna leave
without their patient.

613
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:36,015
We just need to treat her.

614
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:37,642
- Even if she's undocumented?

615
00:24:37,643 --> 00:24:39,769
- All patients, regardless
of immigration status,

616
00:24:39,770 --> 00:24:42,773
have the right to emergency
care under EMTALA.

617
00:24:43,774 --> 00:24:45,650
- Pranita is next in line
for X-ray.

618
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:47,111
- OK, good. Thank you.

619
00:24:48,821 --> 00:24:51,406
- Propofol is down
to 100 mikes per minute.

620
00:24:51,407 --> 00:24:52,824
- Temp is 101.8.

621
00:24:52,825 --> 00:24:54,784
- Great, let's get him
off the ice.

622
00:24:54,785 --> 00:24:56,744
- OK, hands.

623
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:59,123
On my count.
One, two, three.

624
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:03,418
- What's the latest?

625
00:25:03,419 --> 00:25:06,462
- Uh, we got some arm movement.

626
00:25:06,463 --> 00:25:08,173
- That's a good sign.

627
00:25:09,967 --> 00:25:13,345
- And pupils are
minimally reactive.

628
00:25:14,555 --> 00:25:16,973
- Plantars are downgoing.

629
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:19,143
- All encouraging signs.

630
00:25:21,145 --> 00:25:23,187
Any luck getting a lawyer
for our detainee?

631
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:24,814
- Uh, no.

632
00:25:24,815 --> 00:25:26,733
- Keep me posted.

633
00:25:26,734 --> 00:25:28,151
- Yeah.

634
00:25:28,152 --> 00:25:31,196
[beeping]

635
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:34,741
- That's a pretty bracelet.

636
00:25:34,742 --> 00:25:36,117
- [sighs]

637
00:25:36,118 --> 00:25:38,162
My daughter made it for me.

638
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:41,330
She doesn't know where I am.

639
00:25:41,331 --> 00:25:44,168
I just want her to know
that I'm OK.

640
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:48,379
- You seriously won't let her
make a phone call?

641
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:50,798
- Not until she's processed.

642
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:52,342
- Unbelievable.

643
00:25:54,011 --> 00:25:56,679
- Thanks, and just let me know
when she gets back.

644
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:58,014
Uh, one other thing.

645
00:25:58,015 --> 00:26:00,892
Uh, do you have a resident
named Adam?

646
00:26:00,893 --> 00:26:03,186
I was wondering if I could get
his parents' phone number.

647
00:26:03,187 --> 00:26:04,395
- Nope!
- I--

648
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:06,022
- Red phone is
for emergencies only.

649
00:26:06,023 --> 00:26:08,192
- This is kind of an emergency.

650
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:11,070
Sorry. Bye.

651
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:14,030
- Hey, Mel, we need an R3

652
00:26:14,031 --> 00:26:15,531
to supervise a reduction
in North 4.

653
00:26:15,532 --> 00:26:17,701
Are you free?
- Uh, I guess.

654
00:26:18,577 --> 00:26:20,411
- Should we move
the deceased woman

655
00:26:20,412 --> 00:26:22,371
in Central 9 to viewing?

656
00:26:22,372 --> 00:26:24,040
- Uh, no, let's leave
the husband in there

657
00:26:24,041 --> 00:26:26,209
for a little while longer.
- We need the room.

658
00:26:26,210 --> 00:26:28,211
- We're not moving her yet!

659
00:26:28,212 --> 00:26:29,629
- OK, sorry.

660
00:26:29,630 --> 00:26:31,340
- [sighs]
I'm gonna do a room check.

661
00:26:32,633 --> 00:26:35,218
- Pedes ICU says
they'll have a bed soon.

662
00:26:35,219 --> 00:26:36,969
- OK.

663
00:26:36,970 --> 00:26:40,015
[indistinct chatter]

664
00:26:41,308 --> 00:26:43,226
- So what do we think?

665
00:26:43,227 --> 00:26:44,727
- About what?

666
00:26:44,728 --> 00:26:46,854
- The mom of our
heatstroke kid.

667
00:26:46,855 --> 00:26:48,397
- Uh, that is not our job.

668
00:26:48,398 --> 00:26:50,566
That is what CYF is for.

669
00:26:50,567 --> 00:26:52,360
- So you think
it was on purpose?

670
00:26:52,361 --> 00:26:54,570
- No, I did not say that.

671
00:26:54,571 --> 00:26:55,905
- I just don't buy it.

672
00:26:55,906 --> 00:26:57,448
She lost her kid at home?

673
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:58,741
Plus, she just looks guilty.

674
00:26:58,742 --> 00:27:00,452
Has anyone seen her cry?

675
00:27:01,912 --> 00:27:03,704
- People don't always
respond to trauma

676
00:27:03,705 --> 00:27:05,456
the way you expect them to.

677
00:27:05,457 --> 00:27:07,917
Stay focused on the kid.

678
00:27:07,918 --> 00:27:10,419
[rapid beeping]

679
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:13,131
- BP 78 over 42, sats 87.

680
00:27:13,132 --> 00:27:16,008
- You having some pain
again, Mr. Green?

681
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:17,844
Mr. Green?
- This one's yours?

682
00:27:17,845 --> 00:27:20,555
- Yeah, a kidney stone.
Possible vasovagal.

683
00:27:20,556 --> 00:27:22,306
- Can't assume that.
We need some help here!

684
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:23,474
Does he have an IV?

685
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:25,768
- N-no, he didn't need one.

686
00:27:25,769 --> 00:27:28,187
- Hypotensive and hypoxic.

687
00:27:28,188 --> 00:27:29,647
- Clear a trauma room.

688
00:27:29,648 --> 00:27:31,149
- Yeah.

689
00:27:31,150 --> 00:27:33,693
- Uh, he was just waiting on
his discharge meds.

690
00:27:33,694 --> 00:27:35,362
Pain-free.

691
00:27:36,488 --> 00:27:38,197
- A few more patients
are gone from chairs.

692
00:27:38,198 --> 00:27:40,324
South 15 took off too.

693
00:27:40,325 --> 00:27:41,617
- History of renal colic.

694
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:43,494
Heme-positive urine.
BP crashing.

695
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:45,913
- Heme-positive urine doesn't
always mean kidney stone.

696
00:27:45,914 --> 00:27:48,291
Two antecubital lines,
biggest ones we've got,

697
00:27:48,292 --> 00:27:53,004
E-FAST, and let's get two units
of whole blood hung, please.

698
00:27:53,005 --> 00:27:54,131
Good.

699
00:27:55,924 --> 00:27:58,092
Who worked up this patient?
- I did.

700
00:27:58,093 --> 00:28:00,595
Ultrasound showed
dilated ureter a--

701
00:28:00,596 --> 00:28:02,013
and mild left hydronephrosis

702
00:28:02,014 --> 00:28:04,140
consistent with his history
of renal colic.

703
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,641
- What about the aorta?

704
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:07,602
- I didn't look at the aorta.

705
00:28:07,603 --> 00:28:09,604
- Who did you present to?
- Dr. Mohan.

706
00:28:09,605 --> 00:28:11,314
- You said the rest
of the ultrasound was normal.

707
00:28:11,315 --> 00:28:13,441
- I meant that the other
kidney was normal.

708
00:28:13,442 --> 00:28:15,568
- [sighs]
- [sighs]

709
00:28:15,569 --> 00:28:17,320
8-centimeter triple-A
with massive free fluid.

710
00:28:17,321 --> 00:28:19,155
- Ruptured aortic aneurysm.
He's bleeding out.

711
00:28:19,156 --> 00:28:20,489
- OK, go with the MTP.

712
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:21,908
- 16-gauge in the left AC.

713
00:28:21,909 --> 00:28:24,160
Two units whole blood
on the infuser.

714
00:28:24,161 --> 00:28:25,161
[rapid beeping]

715
00:28:25,162 --> 00:28:27,163
- Assisting ventilations.

716
00:28:27,164 --> 00:28:28,664
Resps are agonal.

717
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:30,876
- OK, who wants to intubate?

718
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,587
Javadi?
- Sure.

719
00:28:34,588 --> 00:28:36,214
- OK, call for six more units
of whole blood.

720
00:28:36,215 --> 00:28:37,882
Eusebio, call surgery.

721
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:40,676
If we stay ahead of him,
we might get him up to the OR.

722
00:28:40,677 --> 00:28:42,053
Here you go.

723
00:28:42,054 --> 00:28:44,723
[rapid beeping]

724
00:28:56,026 --> 00:28:57,526
- We're lightening up
his sedation

725
00:28:57,527 --> 00:29:00,154
to see if he has
any purposeful movement.

726
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:03,407
If so, that will be
an encouraging sign.

727
00:29:03,408 --> 00:29:05,244
- He'll be back to normal?

728
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,162
- There's no certainty

729
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:10,873
as to how much recovery
Micah will have.

730
00:29:10,874 --> 00:29:15,086
His response over
the next 24 hours will tell.

731
00:29:15,087 --> 00:29:19,548
There is a chance
of cognitive impairment,

732
00:29:19,549 --> 00:29:22,718
but also a chance
of meaningful recovery.

733
00:29:22,719 --> 00:29:25,847
- Dr. Al-Hashimi,
the patient in 22 needs you.

734
00:29:27,557 --> 00:29:29,601
- I will be right back.

735
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:46,826
- I'm in. Bag him.

736
00:29:46,827 --> 00:29:48,077
- Nicely done. Good job.

737
00:29:48,078 --> 00:29:49,412
- Unit three is up and running.

738
00:29:49,413 --> 00:29:50,746
- I've got a 16-gauge EJ.

739
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:52,373
- That one goes
on the rapid infuser.

740
00:29:52,374 --> 00:29:53,749
- Good end tidal waveform.

741
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:56,085
[rapid beeping]

742
00:29:56,086 --> 00:29:58,129
- Strong radial pulse.
That's a very good sign.

743
00:29:58,130 --> 00:30:00,256
- BP's up. 86 over 52.

744
00:30:00,257 --> 00:30:01,424
- Some progress.

745
00:30:01,425 --> 00:30:03,259
How about 2 grams TXA?
- Yeah.

746
00:30:03,260 --> 00:30:05,595
What else do we give
after four units of blood?

747
00:30:08,140 --> 00:30:09,307
- Um--
- Calcium gluconate

748
00:30:09,308 --> 00:30:10,599
to counteract hypocalcemia

749
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:12,727
caused by the citrate
anticoagulant.

750
00:30:12,728 --> 00:30:14,437
- Why don't you see
if you can't squeeze a unit

751
00:30:14,438 --> 00:30:16,272
into that peripheral line?

752
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:19,442
[machinery beeping]

753
00:30:19,443 --> 00:30:20,776
- Should somebody place
a central line?

754
00:30:20,777 --> 00:30:22,153
- Long central line
is slower than

755
00:30:22,154 --> 00:30:23,779
short large-bore peripheral.

756
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:24,947
- Flow is proportional

757
00:30:24,948 --> 00:30:27,033
to the fourth power
of the radius.

758
00:30:27,034 --> 00:30:28,617
Physics.

759
00:30:28,618 --> 00:30:30,453
- Right.

760
00:30:30,454 --> 00:30:32,247
- OK.

761
00:30:33,540 --> 00:30:35,167
Bite down on this.

762
00:30:36,460 --> 00:30:37,626
- OK.

763
00:30:37,627 --> 00:30:39,670
I'm stabilizing the humerus.
- All right.

764
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:41,130
After I supinate with traction,

765
00:30:41,131 --> 00:30:43,966
Dr. Whitaker will apply
downward pressure

766
00:30:43,967 --> 00:30:45,384
on the proximal forearm.

767
00:30:45,385 --> 00:30:46,635
- [grunting]
- OK.

768
00:30:46,636 --> 00:30:48,054
This is gonna hurt like hell,
Roberto.

769
00:30:48,055 --> 00:30:49,138
- Mm, mm.

770
00:30:49,139 --> 00:30:51,265
- One, two, three.

771
00:30:51,266 --> 00:30:52,475
- [muffled scream]
[cracking]

772
00:30:52,476 --> 00:30:54,143
[screaming]
- OK.

773
00:30:54,144 --> 00:30:55,978
I'm flexing at the elbow.

774
00:30:55,979 --> 00:30:59,733
- [screaming]

775
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:04,320
- Systolic's down to 68.

776
00:31:04,321 --> 00:31:06,655
- Units five and six
are up and running.

777
00:31:06,656 --> 00:31:08,115
[rapid beeping]

778
00:31:08,116 --> 00:31:10,326
- I'm here for Garcia.
Vascular can't come down.

779
00:31:10,327 --> 00:31:11,660
- Triple A with
hemorrhagic shock.

780
00:31:11,661 --> 00:31:12,828
- Most of these die
in the field.

781
00:31:12,829 --> 00:31:14,163
- He was stable.

782
00:31:14,164 --> 00:31:15,790
Presented with a history
of renal colic.

783
00:31:15,791 --> 00:31:18,334
- And nobody saw
the triple A on ultrasound?

784
00:31:18,335 --> 00:31:19,835
Was this you?

785
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:22,338
- No. It was me.

786
00:31:22,339 --> 00:31:24,590
[flatlining]
- Looks like sinus tach.

787
00:31:24,591 --> 00:31:26,258
- Nope, lost the pulse.
It's PEA.

788
00:31:26,259 --> 00:31:27,718
- Bag him.
Ogilvie, start compressions.

789
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:28,928
- We're having a hard time

790
00:31:28,929 --> 00:31:30,262
staying ahead
of the blood loss.

791
00:31:30,263 --> 00:31:31,931
- Sterile gloves.
Prep for a thoracotomy.

792
00:31:31,932 --> 00:31:34,225
- Dr. Javadi, why don't you
glove up and show Dr. Shamsi

793
00:31:34,226 --> 00:31:35,811
why you belong in the ED?

794
00:31:37,020 --> 00:31:39,188
If we can cross-clamp
the aorta,

795
00:31:39,189 --> 00:31:40,940
we can stop the blood flow
from below the diaphragm.

796
00:31:40,941 --> 00:31:42,567
We can perfuse
the heart and the brain.

797
00:31:45,779 --> 00:31:48,030
- Ten blade.
- Right in there.

798
00:31:48,031 --> 00:31:51,034
[rapid beeping]

799
00:31:55,664 --> 00:31:57,040
- Mayo scissors.

800
00:32:04,381 --> 00:32:05,882
- Rib spreader.

801
00:32:10,929 --> 00:32:12,472
- Satinsky.

802
00:32:13,723 --> 00:32:15,725
- Let me know when you have
enough exposure.

803
00:32:20,063 --> 00:32:21,148
- Right there.

804
00:32:23,859 --> 00:32:25,067
- Do you need me on suction?

805
00:32:25,068 --> 00:32:26,235
- No, there's no blood
in the chest.

806
00:32:26,236 --> 00:32:27,236
It's all in the belly.

807
00:32:27,237 --> 00:32:28,655
Here, keep squeezing.

808
00:32:33,410 --> 00:32:34,911
- Aorta's clamped.

809
00:32:36,121 --> 00:32:37,121
Heart is empty.

810
00:32:37,122 --> 00:32:38,122
- OK, Javadi, get in there.

811
00:32:38,123 --> 00:32:39,416
Internal compressions, go.

812
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:45,588
Put two more units
on the rapid infuser, please.

813
00:32:45,589 --> 00:32:47,466
- That'll be units
seven and eight.

814
00:32:54,097 --> 00:32:55,347
- All right. Neuro's intact.

815
00:32:55,348 --> 00:32:56,932
So we'll do a posterior splint,

816
00:32:56,933 --> 00:32:59,435
a sling, and an ortho referral.

817
00:32:59,436 --> 00:33:00,936
- You know, I'm actually
kind of impressed

818
00:33:00,937 --> 00:33:02,146
you did that without pain meds.

819
00:33:02,147 --> 00:33:03,981
- [chuckles]
Definitely worth it.

820
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:07,109
You know, last year I caught
McCutchen's 300th career homer,

821
00:33:07,110 --> 00:33:09,445
but another fan
stole it from me.

822
00:33:09,446 --> 00:33:11,615
I promised myself I would never
let that happen again.

823
00:33:13,074 --> 00:33:15,159
- Whitaker, can you write
the procedure note?

824
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,619
- Yeah, you already filled
in the T-sheet, so--

825
00:33:16,620 --> 00:33:17,912
- Yeah, well, I'm already here.

826
00:33:17,913 --> 00:33:18,954
- Yeah, I kind of had
a handle--

827
00:33:18,955 --> 00:33:20,331
- I just did everything else,

828
00:33:20,332 --> 00:33:21,499
so can you just
fill out the chart?

829
00:33:21,500 --> 00:33:22,625
- You should probably
finish it.

830
00:33:22,626 --> 00:33:23,918
- Well--
- OK, someone do this!

831
00:33:23,919 --> 00:33:25,670
I don't--I don't--
I don't care who.

832
00:33:27,464 --> 00:33:28,632
- Yeah.

833
00:33:30,467 --> 00:33:32,219
[sighs]

834
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:36,181
[beeping]

835
00:33:37,349 --> 00:33:38,724
- Where's Mrs. Azurmendi?

836
00:33:38,725 --> 00:33:40,309
- She stepped out.

837
00:33:40,310 --> 00:33:41,686
- Stepped out?

838
00:33:46,983 --> 00:33:48,526
- Feels like the heart's
filling back up.

839
00:33:48,527 --> 00:33:50,319
- Let's have a peek.

840
00:33:50,320 --> 00:33:52,571
[steady beeping]

841
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:55,032
- Looks good. Really good.

842
00:33:55,033 --> 00:33:56,785
- Strong radial pulse.

843
00:33:58,328 --> 00:34:00,830
- Moist lap pads.
Prep for transfer.

844
00:34:01,706 --> 00:34:03,832
- Systolic of 94.
That's the best so far.

845
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:05,252
- Can I go with you?

846
00:34:06,545 --> 00:34:08,837
He's my patient.

847
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:10,464
- OK by me.

848
00:34:10,465 --> 00:34:12,217
- Bring two extra units.

849
00:34:14,469 --> 00:34:15,845
- [sighs]

850
00:34:17,389 --> 00:34:19,056
[softly]
ICE is in the building?

851
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:20,349
- Word travels fast. Yeah.

852
00:34:20,350 --> 00:34:22,726
We have a detainee
with a rotator cuff tear.

853
00:34:22,727 --> 00:34:23,978
- Two of our nurses went home.

854
00:34:23,979 --> 00:34:25,187
They have temporary
protected status,

855
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:27,357
but they just don't feel safe.

856
00:34:30,193 --> 00:34:32,528
- Um, I'm really sorry,
Dr. Robby.

857
00:34:32,529 --> 00:34:33,654
I should have checked
the aorta.

858
00:34:33,655 --> 00:34:35,114
- It's an easy one to miss.

859
00:34:35,115 --> 00:34:38,076
Got a heartbeat back, though,
so still some hope.

860
00:34:41,705 --> 00:34:42,746
- I'm sorry too.

861
00:34:42,747 --> 00:34:44,373
I--I should have asked Ogilvie

862
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:45,874
if he'd checked the aorta.

863
00:34:45,875 --> 00:34:48,085
It's--it's my fault.
- It is.

864
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:49,461
You're the senior resident.

865
00:34:49,462 --> 00:34:51,213
You don't look to others.
Others look to you.

866
00:34:51,214 --> 00:34:53,549
- I know. I'm really sorry.
- This is what happens

867
00:34:53,550 --> 00:34:55,551
when you bring your
personal life into work.

868
00:34:55,552 --> 00:34:57,178
Patient almost died.
- I know.

869
00:34:58,555 --> 00:35:01,098
- You have to think of these
walls like a force field.

870
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:02,766
You cannot let anything in.

871
00:35:02,767 --> 00:35:04,560
Your mother's not in here.
She is out there.

872
00:35:04,561 --> 00:35:06,437
You keep everything out there.
That is the key.

873
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:08,772
That is the difference
between the best doctors

874
00:35:08,773 --> 00:35:10,733
and the ones
that don't make it.

875
00:35:10,734 --> 00:35:12,068
- You're right.

876
00:35:13,403 --> 00:35:15,780
Maybe I just don't belong here.

877
00:35:18,199 --> 00:35:19,742
- [sighs]

878
00:35:19,743 --> 00:35:21,452
- Pranita's X-ray results.

879
00:35:21,453 --> 00:35:23,203
No fracture.
- OK.

880
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:25,414
We'll just have Jesse fit her
for a sling, I guess,

881
00:35:25,415 --> 00:35:26,957
and then we have to
discharge her.

882
00:35:26,958 --> 00:35:28,917
- To the immigration guys?

883
00:35:28,918 --> 00:35:30,420
- I'm afraid so.

884
00:35:32,589 --> 00:35:34,798
OK, time for you to go.

885
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:37,343
- I was just having a chat
with Ms. Peters here.

886
00:35:37,344 --> 00:35:39,595
- You can see how busy
this department is, right?

887
00:35:39,596 --> 00:35:40,929
You've been nothing
but a distraction

888
00:35:40,930 --> 00:35:42,598
and a disruption
since you've been here.

889
00:35:42,599 --> 00:35:44,767
I'm already short-staffed,
and I just lost five nurses

890
00:35:44,768 --> 00:35:46,602
and half my environmental
services team

891
00:35:46,603 --> 00:35:48,854
because you walked in.

892
00:35:48,855 --> 00:35:50,939
You know patients come in
here for help, right?

893
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:52,691
Because they're either sick
or they're injured,

894
00:35:52,692 --> 00:35:54,276
and documented or undocumented,

895
00:35:54,277 --> 00:35:56,278
they have a right
to emergency care.

896
00:35:56,279 --> 00:35:58,906
TB, measles, fractures--
none of it's getting treated

897
00:35:58,907 --> 00:36:00,115
'cause everybody's
too scared to come in.

898
00:36:00,116 --> 00:36:01,158
But then they end up
here anyway,

899
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,660
but then it's too fucking late!

900
00:36:02,661 --> 00:36:04,244
So please, for the love of God,
can you just go

901
00:36:04,245 --> 00:36:06,121
wait over there in the room
with your detainee,

902
00:36:06,122 --> 00:36:08,541
so I don't lose any more
patients or staff?

903
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:12,003
- No problem, Doc.

904
00:36:22,472 --> 00:36:24,641
- Mrs. Azurmendi.

905
00:36:26,017 --> 00:36:28,018
Brenda.

906
00:36:28,019 --> 00:36:29,812
Where are you going?

907
00:36:29,813 --> 00:36:31,189
[horn blares]
Brenda!

908
00:36:36,152 --> 00:36:37,569
- [crying]
- OK, OK.

909
00:36:37,570 --> 00:36:39,154
It's OK.

910
00:36:39,155 --> 00:36:40,906
Let's get you back inside
to your son.

911
00:36:40,907 --> 00:36:43,159
It's OK. It's OK.
It's OK. It's OK.

912
00:36:45,745 --> 00:36:48,497
- Come on. She's cleared to go.

913
00:36:48,498 --> 00:36:50,249
- Wait. Hold on.
She needs a sling.

914
00:36:50,250 --> 00:36:51,750
- This will only take a minute.
- We're leaving.

915
00:36:51,751 --> 00:36:53,377
- [whimpers]
- Hey, man, you're hurting her!

916
00:36:53,378 --> 00:36:56,004
[objects clattering]
[shouting]

917
00:36:56,005 --> 00:36:57,756
- Jesus Christ.
What's going on now?

918
00:36:57,757 --> 00:36:59,091
- [screams]
- Robby!

919
00:36:59,092 --> 00:37:00,592
- Help!
[shouting]

920
00:37:00,593 --> 00:37:03,262
- You can't do this!
What are you doing?

921
00:37:03,263 --> 00:37:04,596
- This is bullshit.
- What the hell is going on?

922
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:05,681
- Get your hands off me.
- He hurt her,

923
00:37:05,682 --> 00:37:06,974
and Jesse stepped in!

924
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:08,475
- Robby, I didn't do shit.
- I know.

925
00:37:08,476 --> 00:37:09,977
I know. I'm just gonna--
- [speaking indistinctly]

926
00:37:09,978 --> 00:37:11,687
[indistinct shouting, chatter]

927
00:37:11,688 --> 00:37:13,147
No!
- We gotta go.

928
00:37:13,148 --> 00:37:15,482
- No, don't!
- Come on.

929
00:37:15,483 --> 00:37:17,192
- Don't say anything.
You don't have to say anything.

930
00:37:17,193 --> 00:37:18,193
They can't make you
say anything.

931
00:37:18,194 --> 00:37:19,194
We'll get you an attorney.

932
00:37:19,195 --> 00:37:21,029
I promise we'll get you out.

933
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:22,531
Call the hospital attorney
again.

934
00:37:22,532 --> 00:37:23,907
- No, no!
- Can't believe this shit!

935
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:25,409
- Can you at least tell us
where you're taking them?

936
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:26,702
- No!

937
00:37:26,703 --> 00:37:28,203
- Is there a detention center
near Pittsburgh?

938
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:29,705
That's gotta be where
they're going, right?

939
00:37:29,706 --> 00:37:31,540
- It could be hours
before he's processed.

940
00:37:31,541 --> 00:37:33,500
- I'll stay on it.

941
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:35,544
- What can we do?

942
00:37:35,545 --> 00:37:37,129
- Uh--hey, Javadi!

943
00:37:37,130 --> 00:37:38,964
Javadi, please come back.

944
00:37:38,965 --> 00:37:41,216
Everybody, just go
check on your patients.

945
00:37:41,217 --> 00:37:42,634
Assure them.
Tell them what happened.

946
00:37:42,635 --> 00:37:44,219
But please,
everybody get back to work.

947
00:37:44,220 --> 00:37:45,763
- Who's gonna take
Jesse's patients?

948
00:37:45,764 --> 00:37:47,806
- I can do it, D.
- Thanks, Perlah.

949
00:37:47,807 --> 00:37:49,391
[indistinct chatter]

950
00:37:49,392 --> 00:37:50,976
- Hey, you OK?
- Yeah, I'm OK.

951
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:52,728
Are you OK?
- Yeah.

952
00:37:52,729 --> 00:37:54,563
- The lawyers are tied up
with the cyberattacks upstairs.

953
00:37:54,564 --> 00:37:56,398
They probably won't come down
for a while.

954
00:37:56,399 --> 00:37:58,066
<i>[beeping]</i>

955
00:37:58,067 --> 00:37:59,777
- What's the latest
with the heatstroke kid?

956
00:37:59,778 --> 00:38:01,946
- I sent him up to Pedes ICU.

957
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:08,368
- [softly] What's going on?

958
00:38:08,369 --> 00:38:10,078
- I found her outside,
wandering into the street.

959
00:38:10,079 --> 00:38:11,872
She almost got hit by a truck.

960
00:38:11,873 --> 00:38:13,582
[sighs]
I think it was intentional.

961
00:38:13,583 --> 00:38:15,083
- Christ almighty.

962
00:38:15,084 --> 00:38:16,585
- I told Nurse Kim not
to let her out of her sight.

963
00:38:16,586 --> 00:38:18,754
We need to call a 302
and observe her.

964
00:38:18,755 --> 00:38:20,047
- Danger to self.

965
00:38:20,048 --> 00:38:21,590
- Is she gonna be able
to see her kid?

966
00:38:21,591 --> 00:38:23,634
- Not if she's on
an involuntary psych hold.

967
00:38:23,635 --> 00:38:25,594
- Well, what happens if
he's ready to be discharged

968
00:38:25,595 --> 00:38:26,970
before she is?

969
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:28,806
- Does she have a partner
or a relative we can call?

970
00:38:28,807 --> 00:38:30,224
- I can find out.

971
00:38:30,225 --> 00:38:31,642
- Why don't you and I
talk to her together?

972
00:38:31,643 --> 00:38:33,477
- Sure, I just need
to check on a patient,

973
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:35,771
and I will meet you there.
- OK.

974
00:38:35,772 --> 00:38:38,858
[indistinct chatter]

975
00:38:48,368 --> 00:38:51,162
- Uh, OK.

976
00:38:52,205 --> 00:38:53,539
- Hey, Emma,

977
00:38:53,540 --> 00:38:54,790
have you seen this patient?

978
00:38:54,791 --> 00:38:56,041
- Oh, I--I haven't.

979
00:38:56,042 --> 00:38:57,626
- Oh, she took off
when those ICE guys

980
00:38:57,627 --> 00:38:58,920
arrested your nurse.

981
00:39:01,631 --> 00:39:03,049
- Damn it.

982
00:39:04,133 --> 00:39:06,802
- [whispering]
I tried to get him

983
00:39:06,803 --> 00:39:08,679
to help me in the garden,

984
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:11,474
but he just wanted
to ride his trike.

985
00:39:13,601 --> 00:39:15,644
So I let him.

986
00:39:15,645 --> 00:39:18,146
Every time I looked over,

987
00:39:18,147 --> 00:39:22,402
he was just riding around.

988
00:39:24,779 --> 00:39:27,948
And then he wasn't.

989
00:39:27,949 --> 00:39:31,160
- Have you ever thought
about hurting yourself?

990
00:39:34,455 --> 00:39:35,789
- CBC and blood alcohol are

991
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:37,207
back on your golfer,
Curtis Larson.

992
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:39,293
0.14.
- Copy that.

993
00:39:39,294 --> 00:39:41,545
OK, we'll wait
for the other labs.

994
00:39:41,546 --> 00:39:43,256
He'll need to sleep it off
in the meantime.

995
00:39:44,924 --> 00:39:47,593
- Hey, Gabriel,
can you wait up a sec?

996
00:39:47,594 --> 00:39:49,344
Do you have Duke Ekins'
chest X-ray?

997
00:39:49,345 --> 00:39:50,762
- Yeah.
- How's it look?

998
00:39:50,763 --> 00:39:52,431
- Radiologists still
need to read it.

999
00:39:52,432 --> 00:39:54,142
- Can you pull it up for me?

1000
00:39:58,688 --> 00:40:00,355
Shit.

1001
00:40:00,356 --> 00:40:02,399
- [sighs]
I gotta call the funeral home,

1002
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:03,734
start making arrangements.

1003
00:40:03,735 --> 00:40:04,860
- Or you could slow down,

1004
00:40:04,861 --> 00:40:06,695
take some time for yourself.

1005
00:40:06,696 --> 00:40:08,071
How you doing?

1006
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:10,699
- Oh, you know, been better.

1007
00:40:10,700 --> 00:40:12,701
You spend so much time
with these people,

1008
00:40:12,702 --> 00:40:14,202
you become a part
of their family.

1009
00:40:14,203 --> 00:40:16,371
It's not like it is here,
where patients come and go.

1010
00:40:16,372 --> 00:40:17,873
- Don't stay
for the night shift.

1011
00:40:17,874 --> 00:40:19,541
We got reinforcements
coming in.

1012
00:40:19,542 --> 00:40:20,876
- I'd rather work.

1013
00:40:20,877 --> 00:40:22,210
I don't know if I want
to sit with this at home.

1014
00:40:22,211 --> 00:40:23,378
- Try.
For once, just listen to me.

1015
00:40:23,379 --> 00:40:24,379
Take the night off.

1016
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:25,672
I'll cover for you until

1017
00:40:25,673 --> 00:40:27,215
I can find someone else
to come in.

1018
00:40:27,216 --> 00:40:28,927
Go.
- OK.

1019
00:40:30,094 --> 00:40:31,387
- OK.

1020
00:40:36,392 --> 00:40:38,394
- You think she's gonna be OK?

1021
00:40:39,562 --> 00:40:40,896
- I don't know.

1022
00:40:40,897 --> 00:40:43,231
I just hope she can
forgive herself.

1023
00:40:43,232 --> 00:40:44,651
[bell dings]

1024
00:40:50,823 --> 00:40:54,076
I've noticed some tension
between you and Dr. Santos.

1025
00:40:54,077 --> 00:40:55,494
You two have history?

1026
00:40:55,495 --> 00:40:57,079
- Uh, yeah.

1027
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:58,873
She doesn't like me very much.

1028
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:03,752
Uh...

1029
00:41:03,753 --> 00:41:05,796
we worked together one time.

1030
00:41:05,797 --> 00:41:08,924
I was a pretty big asshole.

1031
00:41:08,925 --> 00:41:11,510
She called me out
on some things that I...

1032
00:41:11,511 --> 00:41:16,098
wasn't ready to face,
and I overreacted.

1033
00:41:16,099 --> 00:41:17,307
I'm gonna talk to her.

1034
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:20,560
I just haven't found
the right time.

1035
00:41:20,561 --> 00:41:21,937
- Good.

1036
00:41:21,938 --> 00:41:23,314
Do.

1037
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:34,658
- Thought you might be in here.

1038
00:41:34,659 --> 00:41:36,118
What's going on?
- [sighs]

1039
00:41:36,119 --> 00:41:38,829
It's just the deposition
and my sister coming in.

1040
00:41:38,830 --> 00:41:40,831
It's been a--a day.

1041
00:41:40,832 --> 00:41:42,165
- Oh.

1042
00:41:42,166 --> 00:41:44,459
Screw the deposition.

1043
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:46,421
Is your sister OK?

1044
00:41:47,547 --> 00:41:49,464
- Yeah, it's just a UTI,

1045
00:41:49,465 --> 00:41:51,133
so meds will clear it up.

1046
00:41:51,134 --> 00:41:53,177
- Well, that's good.

1047
00:41:54,470 --> 00:41:59,141
- She has a boyfriend
she didn't tell me about,

1048
00:41:59,142 --> 00:42:01,476
and other things
she didn't tell me about.

1049
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:03,061
- Well, maybe
she didn't know how.

1050
00:42:03,062 --> 00:42:04,856
- She's having sex.

1051
00:42:06,482 --> 00:42:09,067
Great s-sex.

1052
00:42:09,068 --> 00:42:10,402
And she lied to me.

1053
00:42:10,403 --> 00:42:12,988
I mean, she--she lied
to my face for 6 months.

1054
00:42:12,989 --> 00:42:14,866
My sister is a fucking liar.

1055
00:42:16,576 --> 00:42:18,077
- Did you just curse?

1056
00:42:19,996 --> 00:42:22,497
- It's how I feel.

1057
00:42:22,498 --> 00:42:24,499
- Look, kid,

1058
00:42:24,500 --> 00:42:26,835
I say this with love.

1059
00:42:26,836 --> 00:42:29,713
People got their own reasons
for keeping secrets.

1060
00:42:29,714 --> 00:42:32,174
Most of the time, it's got
nothing to do with you.

1061
00:42:32,175 --> 00:42:35,677
- I've seen "Elf" 164 times.

1062
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:38,847
Becca loves "Elf,"
so we watch "Elf."

1063
00:42:38,848 --> 00:42:40,057
And she's got everything,

1064
00:42:40,058 --> 00:42:41,808
and n--and now
she's got a boyfriend,

1065
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:43,560
and they're gonna fall in love
and they're gonna get married,

1066
00:42:43,561 --> 00:42:45,855
and I'm gonna be
completely alone.

1067
00:42:49,776 --> 00:42:52,361
- Did it feel good
to say that out loud?

1068
00:42:53,696 --> 00:42:54,947
- No.

1069
00:42:56,699 --> 00:43:00,702
- Mel, you're a good egg,

1070
00:43:00,703 --> 00:43:03,914
but this is not about you.

1071
00:43:03,915 --> 00:43:05,082
I learned a long time ago

1072
00:43:05,083 --> 00:43:06,875
to quit feeling
sorry for myself.

1073
00:43:06,876 --> 00:43:07,876
Now come on.

1074
00:43:07,877 --> 00:43:09,504
Pity party's over.

1075
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:19,346
- OK, so this is your heart,

1076
00:43:19,347 --> 00:43:22,015
and these are your lungs.

1077
00:43:22,016 --> 00:43:23,600
- They look OK?
- Yeah.

1078
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:24,851
It's this part right here,

1079
00:43:24,852 --> 00:43:26,353
this space right
between your lungs.

1080
00:43:26,354 --> 00:43:29,106
It's called the mediastinum,
and it is enlarged.

1081
00:43:29,107 --> 00:43:30,899
It is too wide.

1082
00:43:30,900 --> 00:43:32,359
- From what?

1083
00:43:32,360 --> 00:43:34,194
- Can't really tell
from the plain film.

1084
00:43:34,195 --> 00:43:35,529
Could be any number of things.

1085
00:43:35,530 --> 00:43:37,739
- Yeah, stop the bullshit.

1086
00:43:37,740 --> 00:43:39,616
- It could be
an enlarged thyroid.

1087
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:41,910
It could be
enlarged lymph nodes

1088
00:43:41,911 --> 00:43:42,911
from an infection.

1089
00:43:42,912 --> 00:43:45,581
It could possibly be a tumor.

1090
00:43:46,916 --> 00:43:48,792
- You think I have lung cancer?

1091
00:43:48,793 --> 00:43:50,919
- Nope, I don't see that.

1092
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:53,463
But cancer of the lymph nodes
is called lymphoma.

1093
00:43:53,464 --> 00:43:55,590
And there are a lot
of diseases of the aorta,

1094
00:43:55,591 --> 00:43:57,467
which is this big artery
that comes off the heart,

1095
00:43:57,468 --> 00:43:58,635
which can get enlarged

1096
00:43:58,636 --> 00:44:00,428
because of weak spot
in the wall.

1097
00:44:00,429 --> 00:44:05,267
Kind of like a, uh, bubble in
a tire that can have a blowout.

1098
00:44:05,268 --> 00:44:07,853
And the only way to make sure

1099
00:44:07,854 --> 00:44:10,981
is to do a CT scan
of your chest.

1100
00:44:10,982 --> 00:44:12,315
Today.

1101
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:13,985
- How long does that take?

1102
00:44:15,945 --> 00:44:18,364
- A few hours, couple hours.

1103
00:44:19,824 --> 00:44:21,951
- You still gonna be here?

1104
00:44:25,580 --> 00:44:30,168
- Yeah, I would not feel good
about riding if I rushed this.

1105
00:44:33,004 --> 00:44:34,714
- This is important?

1106
00:44:39,135 --> 00:44:40,553
- Hey.

1107
00:44:41,304 --> 00:44:43,471
I think the, uh, labs are back

1108
00:44:43,472 --> 00:44:45,307
on your COPD patient.

1109
00:44:45,308 --> 00:44:46,766
Saw 'em in the rack.

1110
00:44:46,767 --> 00:44:48,435
- Thanks.

1111
00:44:48,436 --> 00:44:49,978
- Uh, look.

1112
00:44:49,979 --> 00:44:51,646
I don't know how to say this.

1113
00:44:51,647 --> 00:44:53,191
Um...

1114
00:44:55,318 --> 00:44:58,820
I know you don't like me,
and--and that's fine.

1115
00:44:58,821 --> 00:45:00,655
You don't have to. I just--

1116
00:45:00,656 --> 00:45:02,324
I want to say I'm sorry

1117
00:45:02,325 --> 00:45:04,326
for being an asshole
on your first day.

1118
00:45:04,327 --> 00:45:06,244
That was completely
inappropriate,

1119
00:45:06,245 --> 00:45:09,331
and if I could take back
what happened,

1120
00:45:09,332 --> 00:45:11,417
I would, but I can't.

1121
00:45:13,502 --> 00:45:14,545
- OK.

1122
00:45:16,005 --> 00:45:17,923
[bell dings]

1123
00:45:17,924 --> 00:45:19,090
OK, I'm sorry, I just--

1124
00:45:19,091 --> 00:45:20,508
I don't buy it.

1125
00:45:20,509 --> 00:45:21,885
Everyone thinks
you're just an addict

1126
00:45:21,886 --> 00:45:23,094
who went to rehab,

1127
00:45:23,095 --> 00:45:24,512
and you've convinced
everyone here

1128
00:45:24,513 --> 00:45:25,722
that you've changed

1129
00:45:25,723 --> 00:45:27,182
and you're owning up
to your mistakes,

1130
00:45:27,183 --> 00:45:28,808
and they welcome you back
with open arms

1131
00:45:28,809 --> 00:45:30,227
because you're still
the golden boy,

1132
00:45:30,228 --> 00:45:31,729
and I think it's bullshit.

1133
00:45:33,022 --> 00:45:34,814
- I'm genuinely sorry.

1134
00:45:34,815 --> 00:45:37,067
And I can promise you,
I have faced my fair share

1135
00:45:37,068 --> 00:45:38,318
of punishment for what I did.

1136
00:45:38,319 --> 00:45:40,695
- You fucking stole drugs
from the hospital.

1137
00:45:40,696 --> 00:45:42,364
Only three people here
actually know that.

1138
00:45:42,365 --> 00:45:44,324
Have you told anyone else
what you did?

1139
00:45:44,325 --> 00:45:45,700
Have you?
- Look.

1140
00:45:45,701 --> 00:45:47,535
I'm just trying to get through
my first day back.

1141
00:45:47,536 --> 00:45:49,037
- You shouldn't even be here!

1142
00:45:49,038 --> 00:45:50,872
I should have reported you
to the state medical board.

1143
00:45:50,873 --> 00:45:53,041
You should have lost your
license and gone to prison.

1144
00:45:53,042 --> 00:45:54,501
- You don't know
what I've been through.

1145
00:45:54,502 --> 00:45:55,752
- What you've been through?

1146
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:57,045
- My wife threatened
to divorce me, OK?

1147
00:45:57,046 --> 00:45:58,380
I almost lost my kids.

1148
00:45:58,381 --> 00:46:00,383
- Yeah, that's what happens
when you fuck up.

1149
00:46:02,218 --> 00:46:03,593
- [sighs]

1150
00:46:03,594 --> 00:46:05,095
You don't have to accept
my apology.

1151
00:46:05,096 --> 00:46:08,015
I just--
I wanted to say it, OK?

1152
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:11,309
- You really want
to atone for your sins?

1153
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,727
Tell everyone here
you stole drugs

1154
00:46:12,728 --> 00:46:14,479
and got kicked out of the ED
because of it.

1155
00:46:14,480 --> 00:46:16,899
Until then, stay out of my way.

1156
00:46:24,240 --> 00:46:27,118
[soft beeping]

1157
00:46:29,078 --> 00:46:30,578
- [gasps]
- Oh, hi.

1158
00:46:30,579 --> 00:46:32,080
- What the fuck?

1159
00:46:32,081 --> 00:46:33,290
- I'm just checking
your vital signs.

1160
00:46:33,291 --> 00:46:34,708
- [grunts]
- Oh.

1161
00:46:34,709 --> 00:46:36,793
- Where am I?

1162
00:46:36,794 --> 00:46:38,253
- Oh!
- What did you do to me?

1163
00:46:38,254 --> 00:46:39,713
- [whimpers]
- Huh?

1164
00:46:39,714 --> 00:46:41,756
- [gasping]
- [grunting]

1165
00:46:41,757 --> 00:46:44,217
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

1166
00:46:44,218 --> 00:46:46,429
<i>♪ ♪</i>

1167
